# $crate_package_name

UniFFI-generated Python bindings for `auki-time`.

The generated package exposes time-transform records, NTP sample helpers,
peer-clock sync state, domain-clock composition, and native session-clock
identity:

```python
import $binding_module_name

sample = $binding_module_name.compute_ntp_sample(
    $binding_module_name.NtpExchange(
        local_send_ns=1000,
        remote_receive_ns=1001050,
        remote_send_ns=1001080,
        local_receive_ns=1130,
    )
)

state = $binding_module_name.ClockSyncState(
    $binding_module_name.default_clock_sync_config()
)
estimate = state.observe(
    $binding_module_name.ClockSyncObservation(
        local_clock_id="peer-a/session-1/monotonic",
        local_clock_hash="hash-a",
        remote_clock_id="peer-b/session-7/monotonic",
        remote_clock_hash="hash-b",
        sample=sample,
    )
)
```

Host clocks, registry-entry construction, and the sampler thread are native
APIs. Browser JavaScript bindings expose only the pure math and stateful
selection surface.
